From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:59:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: play command lists back, and keep what they recorded
 where it can be found.

Office's NetUI records its icons and text into command lists and draws
those onto its surfaces, and none of it reached the screen: drawing a
command list was an unhandled image, and EndDraw on one as a target
failed with E_NOTIMPL.  DrawImage now plays a closed list back onto the
context, under the context's transform moved to the target offset and
clipped to the image rectangle, through a command sink of its own;
what the list set -- transform, modes, tags, text parameters -- does not
outlast it.  EndDraw on a list reports what drawing into it came to.

Once that drew, NetUI's labels came out as the wrong characters.  The
recorded glyph runs, bitmap and image rectangles and opacity masks kept
pointers to data inside the list's buffer, and the buffer is
reallocated as the list grows, leaving every such pointer of an earlier
command dangling.  The commands now keep where their data is from
themselves, and a command's data is turned back into pointers as it is
played; commands also start aligned.

As the tests have it on Windows: closing a list that was never drawn to
succeeds, closing one that is a context's target makes the context
target nothing, and a list made on one device cannot be the target of a
context of another.  The todos for those now pass, and a new test of
playing a list back, one grown after a bitmap was recorded, passes on
Windows as here.

IsDxgiFormatSupported answers for the formats Direct2D takes that the
device can sample, rather than for none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 775f583c5d11ce51d7df25854ff69808a6814c5b)

diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
index c6ab60c1bc4..d9cc2eeb6a4 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
@@ -392,6 +392,26 @@ static BOOL format_supported(const D2D1_PIXEL_FORMAT *format)
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/* whether Direct2D takes the format, with any alpha mode */
+BOOL d2d_dxgi_format_supported(DXGI_FORMAT format)
+{
+    static const D2D1_ALPHA_MODE modes[] =
+    {
+        D2D1_ALPHA_MODE_PREMULTIPLIED, D2D1_ALPHA_MODE_STRAIGHT, D2D1_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE,
+    };
+    D2D1_PIXEL_FORMAT pixel_format;
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    pixel_format.format = format;
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(modes); ++i)
+    {
+        pixel_format.alphaMode = modes[i];
+        if (format_supported(&pixel_format))
+            return TRUE;
+    }
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 static void d2d_bitmap_init(struct d2d_bitmap *bitmap, struct d2d_device_context *context,
         ID3D11Resource *resource, D2D1_SIZE_U size, const D2D1_BITMAP_PROPERTIES1 *desc)
 {
diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/command_list.c b/dlls/d2d1/command_list.c
index 6c830d2660e..3f7603c1c03 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/command_list.c
